   "id": "pmt/pure-core-1/ch8/q9",
   "question": "<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M=\\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;a&amp;4\\\\1&amp;-1&amp;-1\\\\-1&amp;2&amp;-1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> is a constant.</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li>For which values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> does the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M\"></span> have an inverse? <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M\"></span> is non-singular,</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"2\"><li>find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M^{-1}\"></span> in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol></li><li>Prove by induction that for all positive integers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\"></span>,<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}3&amp;0\\\\6&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}^n=\\begin{pmatrix}3^n&amp;0\\\\3\\left(3^n-1\\right)&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li></ol>",
